{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789513152,"nonce":"/VZuYmhYPuxB+68j8E9/sZylQOc=","title":"Python: a parameter's default was not one of its inferred types","message":"`def add_option(name, kind=None): ...; add_option(\"-n\", kind=\"int\")` inferred `kind` as str from the one call, and the default `None` was coerced to str at entry: TypeError \"expected str instance, NoneType found\". A default is a value the parameter takes whether or not a call leaves it out; the inferred type now starts from the default's type. Found by the speed harness's optparse shim once methods were typed by their calls.","files":null}]}